MH, Offord OR, Szatmari P, Rae-Grant N, Crawford J.</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Chronic illness and functional limitation in Ontario children: Findings of the Ontario Child Health Study</article-title><source>Medical Association Journal</source><year>1986</year><volume>135</volume><fpage>761</fpage><lpage>767</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nicholas</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The lived experience of mothers caring for a child with End Stage Renal Disease.</article-title><source>Social Work</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>Toronto , University of Toronto</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nicholas</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Richardson A</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Struggles, strengths and strategies: The lived experience of healthy siblings of children with End Stage Renal Disease.</article-title><source>Childhood and Youth: A Universal Odyssey</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>Edmonton , Kanata Learning Company Ltd</publisher-name><fpage>236</fpage><lpage>248</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Otley</surname><given-names>AT</given-names><suffix>Griffiths AM, Sherman PM, Smith C, Avolio J, Munk M, Nicholas D.</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>The IMPACT questionnaire: A valid measure of health related quality of life in pediatric inflammatory bowel disease.</article-title><source>Journal of Pediatric Gastroenterology and Nutrition</source><year>2002</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>557</fpage><lpage>563</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12394384</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00005176-200210000-00018</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gubrium</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><source>Analysing field reality</source><year>1988</year><publisher-name> Newbury Park: CA , Sage</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McCracken</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Long Interview</source><year>1988</year><publisher-name>Thousand Oaks , Sage</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Lincoln</collab><collab>Guba</collab></person-group><source>Naturalistic inquiry.</source><year>1985</year><publisher-name>Beverly Hills, CA , Sage</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Otley</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Griffiths</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hale</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kugathasan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Pfefferkorn</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mezoff</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosh</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Tolia</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Markowitz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mack</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Oliva-Hemker</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wyllie</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Rothbaum</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Bousvaros</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Del Rosario</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Blanchard</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Hyams</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Pediatric</surname><given-names>IBDCRG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Health-related quality of life in the first year after a diagnosis of pediatric inflammatory bowel disease</article-title><source>Inflammatory Bowel Diseases</source><year>2006</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>684</fpage><lpage>691</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16917222</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00054725-200608000-00003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van der Zaag-Loonen</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Grootenhuis</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Last</surname><given-names>BF</given-names></name><name><surname>Derkx</surname><given-names>HH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Coping strategies and quality of life of adolescents with inflammatory bowel disease</article-title><source>Quality of Life Research</source><year>2004</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>1011</fpage><lpage>1019</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15233514</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1023/B:QURE.0000025598.89003.0c</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nicholas</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Koller</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Picone</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fostering childhood participation in health care:  Grandparents' perspectives on children's involvement in the treatment of pediatric end stage renal disease.</article-title><source>Journal of Nephrology Social Work</source><year>2004</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>11</fpage><lpage>12</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Quittner</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>DiGirolamo</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Michel</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Eigen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Parental response to cystic fibrosis:  A contextual analysis of the diagnosis phase.</article-title><source>Journal of Pediatric Psychology</source><year>1992</year><volume>17</volume><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1484333</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shepanski</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hurd</surname><given-names>LB</given-names></name><name><surname>Culton</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Markowitz</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Mamula</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Baldassano</surname><given-names>RN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Health-related quality of life improves in children and adolescents with inflammatory bowel disease after attending a camp sponsored by the Crohn's and Colitis Foundation of America</article-title><source>Inflammatory Bowel Diseases</source><year>2005</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>164</fpage><lpage>170</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15677910</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00054725-200502000-00010</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>